      "timestampEdited": null,
      "callEndedTimestamp": null,
      "isPinned": false,
      "content": "since lef already specifies geometric constraints, what stops foundries from encoding all manufacturable geometry constraints solely within lef files so as to not have a non-standard design rule manual. similar for lib and electrical properties.\n\n\nis there a technical reason for the lef standard to not be able to encode all types of drm rules?",
      "author": {
        "id": "488155070052171816",
        "name": "rahulbhagwat",
        "discriminator": "0000",
        "nickname": "rahulbhagwat",
        "color": null,
        "isBot": false,
        "roles": [],
        "avatarUrl": "2026-11_media/e69d5a0ef16fab73702f739d1fde6389-BE72C.png"
