    {
      "id": "1567980190813003837",
      "type": "Default",
      "timestamp": "2026-11-05T19:13:29.153+00:00",
      "timestampEdited": null,
      "callEndedTimestamp": null,
      "isPinned": false,
      "content": "\"be extended\" ... well if you go with extension then everything is possible ... of course. you could extend LEF with a turing complete language.\n\nBut as the current spec, it's not even close to being able to describe DRC rules ... it can barely even describe the min subset for routing ... even then some of the rules described in the LEF are not the actual rule but some more restrictive variation because you can't describe the actual rule.",
      "author": {
        "id": "596068704471482370",
        "name": "246tnt",
        "discriminator": "0000",
        "nickname": "tnt",
        "color": null,
